messages:
emma: FYI I opened a PR to tidy up a bunch of SDK snippets that were causing confusion around streaming + pagination + retries. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4123
raj: thanks — which snippets are affected?
sasha: saw Python, TypeScript, and Go. Go leaks context and doesn't close stream; Python example doesn't demonstrate resuming a partial page on retry; TS lacks jitter in retry wrapper.
emma: correct. kept changes small and documented the migration path for v1->v2 SDK breaking behavior.
raj: can you paste the old Go snippet here?
sasha: old snippet from docs:
```go
resp, err := client.Stream(ctx, req)
if err != nil {
  return err
}
for e := range resp.Events {
  fmt.Println(e.Text)
}
// no Close() or cancel
```
sasha: proposed fix in PR:
```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(ctx)
defer cancel()
resp, err := client.Stream(ctx, req)
if err != nil {
  return err
}
defer resp.Close()
for {
  ev, ok := resp.Next()
  if !ok { break }
  fmt.Println(ev.Text)
}
```
emma: TS change uses async iterator + a tiny retry wrapper showing exponential backoff + jitter. snippet:
```ts
async function process() {
  for await (const chunk of client.stream(req)) {
    // handle chunk
  }
}
// retry uses base=100ms, factor=2, max=5s with jitter
```
jordan: can we add a minimal pytest for the Python pagination case that mocks a partial page error and asserts the retry resumes correctly? that will prevent regression.
raj: good idea. I'll add a test under sdk-examples/tests if you want it in the same PR, emma.
emma: please add it in the PR so reviewers can run CI against it. I'm also adding a short migration note and a link fix (old redirecting docs link).
docs-bot: linked PR #4123 to DOCS-298 and assigned reviewers @raj @sasha. CI: pending.
raj: nit — clarify per-call timeout vs client/session timeout in the Python snippet. small comment.
emma: updated, pushed. also added an inline tip about handling partial pages when using retries (store page token before reading items).
sasha: LGTM from infra side once tests pass; left one comment about backoff constants.
emma: will squash and merge after green CI and approvals. thanks for the quick review! :sparkles:
docs-bot: CI status: pending — will post result when done.
